// This process's own id (`getpid()`/`GetCurrentProcessId()`, a compiler-
// emitted prelude wrapper - see codegen.fn's write_prelude). A bare
// declaration, matching every other `std.c.*` module: codegen recognizes
// any bodyless node declared under `std/c/*.fn` and skips generating a
// competing forward-declared prototype for it, so the compiler's own
// prelude definition (not this file) stays the sole source of truth.
//
// Not exposed through `std.sys`/a higher-level wrapper: nothing else in
// the standard library needs a process id yet, and Fun emits every public
// function of an imported module whether or not anything actually calls
// it, so a binding added to a module the compiler's own source already
// imports (like `std.sys`) would make `fun build` itself depend on this
// prelude wrapper too. This file has no importers yet, so it stays out of
// that graph until something other than a test helper needs it.
pub fun __fun_process_id() num;
